# MedSync Health, Inc.
## Business Associate Agreement Summary
**Document ID**: LEG-002
**Classification**: Internal - Sales Use
**Version**: 4.0
**Effective**: January 2025

---

## Overview

This document summarizes MedSync's standard Business Associate Agreement (BAA) required for all customers who will process Protected Health Information (PHI) through MedSync services.

---

## Parties & Definitions

### Parties

| Party | Role | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| Covered Entity | Customer | Healthcare provider, health plan, or clearinghouse |
| Business Associate | MedSync | Service provider handling PHI |

### Key Definitions

| Term | Definition |
|------|------------|
| Protected Health Information (PHI) | Individually identifiable health information |
| Electronic PHI (ePHI) | PHI in electronic form |
| Breach | Unauthorized acquisition, access, use, or disclosure |
| Security Incident | Attempted or successful unauthorized access |
| Minimum Necessary | Limiting PHI to what is needed |

---

## Permitted Uses & Disclosures

### Permitted Purposes

| Purpose | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Treatment | Care coordination, referral management |
| Payment | Claims, billing, eligibility |
| Health Care Operations | Quality improvement, case management |
| As Required by Law | Legal obligations |
| As Directed | By Covered Entity in writing |

### Prohibited Uses

MedSync may NOT use or disclose PHI for:
- Marketing (without authorization)
- Sale of PHI
- Genetic information for underwriting
- Any purpose not specified in BAA

